      "source_document": "890045",
      "original_line": 229,
      "text": "The other argument was that the order for recovery of possession was unwarranted as in fact there had been a consent of the respondents to the assignment in favour of the appellant. It is said that the consent was given by a clause in the lease under which Allen Berry & Co. held which reads as follows:--",
